        'The MECHANISM (attributed): mood rides the body — circadian rise/fall, sleep loss weakens emotional control, hunger/blood sugar move mood, stress hormones surge/ebb, and both sexes have hormonal cycles (incl. the monthly cycle for many women). Two cautions: sex differences are real but SMALLER + more overlapping than stereotypes (individuals vary more than groups); and describing the body does not excuse the sin.',
        'The WORD: emotions God-given and real (Jesus wept John 11:35 / Matt 26:38 / Ecc 3:4); God cared for Elijah’s BODY first — sleep + food before the still small voice (1 Kings 19:5,7; Ps 127:2; Mark 6:31); STEWARD by (a) bringing it to God not burying it (Psalm 42:11/62:8/1 Pet 5:7/Phil 4:6-7), (b) ruling the spirit not obeying the feeling (Proverbs 16:32/25:28/Luke 21:19), self-control as FRUIT (Galatians 5:22-23/2 Tim 1:7).',
