      howToRun: 'Open in prayer + read the Scripture (3): read Luke 10:17-20 aloud slowly — ask, "which verse surprises you most?" | The big idea, in your own words (10): the promise (v. 19, delegated authority over ALL the enemy\'s power) and the pivot (v. 20, the better joy); use the keys-on-the-belt picture. | Go deeper (10): Psalm 91:13 echo; what serpents/scorpions are (and are not — Luke 4:12); the fight\'s real address (Ephesians 6:12); submit-then-resist (James 4:7); from-victory (Colossians 2:15; 1 John 4:4). | Reflect together (10): the discussion prompts — land hardest on where each person\'s joy is anchored. | Take it with you (2): each person names their "basement door" and trades power-joy for Book-joy this week.',
