      howToRun: 'Prayer + the anchor (5): open in prayer; read Psalm 139:14 and Proverbs 25:2 aloud (KJV). | The artifact (10): tell the story plainly — a DNA strand taught to glow when lead is in the water; mark which figures are "as reported," which keeps us honest. | Whose code (10): Psalm 139:14-16 and Colossians 1:17 — they read a language they did not write; wonder runs up. | The search (10): Proverbs 25:2 and Job 28:1-3,12,28 — concealment and search are both proper, and wisdom is the fear of the LORD, not the patent. | The mirror (15): each person names one "hidden lead" — an invisible thing quietly harming them or those they keep — and prays Psalm 139:23-24 over it. | Stewardship (5): 1 Corinthians 6:19-20 and Genesis 2:15 — detection serves protection; dominion is keeping. | Send-off (5): seek truth "as for hid treasures" and you will "understand the fear of the LORD" (Proverbs 2:4-5).',
