      howToRun: 'Prayer + the anchor (5): open in prayer; read Isaiah 6:3 and Revelation 22:11 aloud (KJV). | The title (5): the LORD of HOSTS, not "Host" — Sabaoth, the armies of heaven (1 Samuel 17:45). | The two ways (15): Psalms 1:6; Matthew 7:13-14; Proverbs 15:26; Isaiah 55:7 — righteous or wicked, thoughts included, no third. | Time and the seal (10): Hebrews 9:27; Revelation 22:11; 2 Corinthians 6:2 — the window closes; now is the day. | The open door (10): honestly, few are chosen (Matthew 22:14) — and honestly, "whosoever will" (Revelation 22:17); the chosen must choose (Joshua 24:15). | Why not feelings (10): Romans 8:7; Jeremiah 17:9; Proverbs 16:2 — the flesh is self-deceived; prioritize His will (Matthew 6:33). | The remedy (5): the Mind of Christ modeled by the Son (1 Corinthians 2:16; John 5:19). | Send-off (5): while it is still "time," choose His way, present the living sacrifice (Romans 12:1).',
