      howToRun: 'Prayer + the anchor (5): read Genesis 18:25 and Leviticus 19:15 aloud (KJV). | Recap (10): last week\'s just weight — where did we verify before we spoke? | Teach the arc (15): the Just Judge (Genesis 18:25; Romans 2:11) -> the law for every bench (Leviticus 19:15; Deuteronomy 16:19) -> real partiality is sin, named (Proverbs 17:15; Acts 10:34; the USSC + verified case) -> a just weight for the numbers, verify not inflate (Proverbs 18:17; 1 Thessalonians 5:21) -> plead the cause (Proverbs 31:8-9; Amos 5:24) -> not vengeance, one blood (Romans 12:21; Acts 17:26) -> the final court (Psalms 82:1; Ecclesiastes 12:14). | Do-it-now (20): each names one justice claim they have shared or nearly shared without checking, and one wronged person or cause they could plead for. | Discussion (15): the prompts below. | Send-off (5): verify one claim this week before you repeat it.',
      discussionPrompts: [
        'Where were you pulled to a sweeping verdict or a flat dismissal on this story? What does holding both tiers — name the real injustice AND verify the numbers (Proverbs 17:15; 1 Thessalonians 5:21) — change about how you would speak of it?',
        'The disparity is real; some of the framing was overstated. Why does "an inflated truth is handed its own dismissal" matter — and how does a just weight for WORDS (Exodus 23:1; Proverbs 18:17) actually SERVE the wronged rather than betray them?',
        'Yahweh judges the judges and every secret thing (Psalms 82:1; Ecclesiastes 12:14). How does that both comfort the wronged and warn every one of us — and who is one person "appointed to destruction" (Proverbs 31:8) you could plead for this week?',
      ],
