      howToRun: 'Prayer + the anchor (5): read Proverbs 28:1 and 28:13 aloud (KJV). | Recap (10): last week\'s real Champion - where did we choose life and think like the Father? | Teach the arc (20): guilt flees / righteousness stands (28:1) -> clear conscience kept by integrity: confess, truth, grow from failure (28:13; Ephesians 4:25; Proverbs 24:16) -> imputed righteousness (2 Corinthians 5:21) -> the Lion of Judah (Revelation 5:5) -> live-or-die His GOOD will (Romans 14:8; Romans 8:28) -> fear not (2 Timothy 1:7) -> He leads and finishes (Hebrews 12:2) -> abide/train the mind (Philippians 4:8) -> suffer with Him to reign (John 11:35; 2 Timothy 2:12) -> love enemies, the Blood makes family (Matthew 5:44; Ephesians 2:13) -> discern the destroyer (John 10:10; Matthew 10:16) -> boldness to speak and that lasts (Acts 4:29-31; Hebrews 4:16). | Do-it-now (20): each names ONE fault they have been covering (confess and forsake it - Proverbs 28:13), ONE failure to learn from and adjust, ONE fear to surrender (\'live or die, I am the Lord\'s; His will is good\'), ONE enemy to love, and ONE destroyer to discern. | Discussion (15): the prompts below. | Send-off (5): keep the account clear by truth, love the redeemable, discern the destroyer, and let the Author and Finisher lead.',
