    lesson: 'HIS KINGS — reigning under the King of kings. This flows straight out of the previous lesson: the bold righteous are made royalty, and the whole question is WHOSE. ONE — HIS KINGS ARE BOLD, AND THEY ARE HIS. Made, never self-made: "And hath made us kings and priests unto God and his Father; to him be glory and dominion for ever and ever. Amen." (Revelation 1:6); "But ye are a chosen generation, a royal priesthood, an holy nation, a peculiar people; that ye should shew forth the praises of him who hath called you out of darkness into his marvellous light" (1 Peter 2:9). Kings, yes. But HIS kings, and the possessive is the whole lesson. TWO — TWO PATHS, AND THE TELL IS NOT WHAT YOU CALL HIM. "Enter ye in at the strait gate: for wide is the gate, and broad is the way, that leadeth to destruction, and many there be which go in thereat" (Matthew 7:13); "Because strait is the gate, and narrow is the way, which leadeth unto life, and few there be that find it." (Matthew 7:14). And the test of which road you are on is simple and uncomfortable: "And why call ye me, Lord, Lord, and do not the things which I say?" (Luke 6:46). So choose deliberately: "choose you this day whom ye will serve... but as for me and my house, we will serve the LORD." (Joshua 24:15); "For the LORD knoweth the way of the righteous: but the way of the ungodly shall perish." (Psalms 1:6). Being your own king IS the broad way. It does not feel like rebellion from the inside; it feels like independence. THREE — YOU CANNOT BE HIS KING UNLESS. There is an unless, and it is stated twice over. No entry without new birth: "Verily, verily, I say unto thee, Except a man be born again, he cannot see the kingdom of God." (John 3:3); and you become His by confessing Him Lord: "That if thou shalt confess with thy mouth the Lord Jesus, and shalt believe in thine heart that God hath raised him from the dead, thou shalt be saved." (Romans 10:9). And you reign only by first serving, which Jesus states as a reversal of how it works everywhere else: "whosoever will be great among you, let him be your minister" (Matthew 20:26); "And whosoever will be chief among you, let him be your servant" (Matthew 20:27). A king under the King bows before he reigns: "And hast made us unto our God kings and priests: and we shall reign on the earth." (Revelation 5:10). FOUR — THE KING OF KINGS, AND WHAT HIS KINGS DO WITH THEIR CROWNS. "And he hath on his vesture and on his thigh a name written, KING OF KINGS, AND LORD OF LORDS." (Revelation 19:16); "the blessed and only Potentate, the King of kings, and Lord of lords" (1 Timothy 6:15). And the picture of what crowned beings do in His presence settles the posture: "The four and twenty elders fall down before him that sat on the throne, and worship him that liveth for ever and ever, and cast their crowns before the throne" (Revelation 4:10). Authority held in worship, not in pride. FIVE — LIFE AND DEATH IN THE POWER OF THE TONGUE. A king\'s word carries weight, which cuts both ways: "Death and life are in the power of the tongue: and they that love it shall eat the fruit thereof." (Proverbs 18:21); "A divine sentence is in the lips of the king: his mouth transgresseth not in judgment." (Proverbs 16:10). So speak life and truth, never confusion and never lies. SIX — CREATING WEALTH IS THE GOAL, YAHWEH\'S WAY, NOT CONFUSION. This needs saying plainly because it is so often taught badly in both directions. Wealth is a covenant assignment with a stated purpose: "But thou shalt remember the LORD thy God: for it is he that giveth thee power to get wealth, that he may establish his covenant which he sware unto thy fathers" (Deuteronomy 8:18). And its Author is order rather than chaos: "For God is not the author of confusion, but of peace, as in all churches of the saints." (1 Corinthians 14:33). The blessing arrives without a hidden cost: "The blessing of the LORD, it maketh rich, and he addeth no sorrow with it." (Proverbs 10:22). And obedience is what puts His kings at the head: "And the LORD shall make thee the head, and not the tail... if that thou hearken unto the commandments of the LORD thy God" (Deuteronomy 28:13). Wealth Yahweh\'s Way is stewardship under covenant. It is not confusion, and it is not greed with a verse attached. SEVEN — WINNING SOULS, BECAUSE SOULS RESPECT EXCELLENCE. The highest yield is not the money; it is the people. "The fruit of the righteous is a tree of life; and he that winneth souls is wise." (Proverbs 11:30). And excellence is what opens the door — an excellent spirit lifted a captive over an empire: "Then this Daniel was preferred above the presidents and princes, because an excellent spirit was in him" (Daniel 6:3). So the work itself is done for an audience of One: "And whatsoever ye do, do it heartily, as to the Lord, and not unto men" (Colossians 3:23); and it is meant to be visible: "Let your light so shine before men, that they may see your good works, and glorify your Father which is in heaven." (Matthew 5:16). We are standing in for someone: "Now then we are ambassadors for Christ, as though God did beseech you by us: we pray you in Christ’s stead, be ye reconciled to God." (2 Corinthians 5:20). Excellence is evangelism, because kings represent the King whether or not they mean to. EIGHT — THE NECESSARY SKILL, DRAWN FROM HIS WORD. The way, the truth and the life is a Person: "Jesus saith unto him, I am the way, the truth, and the life: no man cometh unto the Father, but by me." (John 14:6). And the skill is His Word handled rightly: "Study to shew thyself approved unto God, a workman that needeth not to be ashamed, rightly dividing the word of truth." (2 Timothy 2:15); searched daily and tested rather than swallowed — "they received the word with all readiness of mind, and searched the scriptures daily, whether those things were so." (Acts 17:11). The Word furnishes for the whole job: "All scripture is given by inspiration of God, and is profitable for doctrine, for reproof, for correction, for instruction in righteousness: That the man of God may be perfect, throughly furnished unto all good works." (2 Timothy 3:16-17). The wisdom itself is issued from His mouth: "For the LORD giveth wisdom: out of his mouth cometh knowledge and understanding." (Proverbs 2:6). And the mind is remade by it (Romans 12:2). NINE — AND THE DESTINATION IS ALREADY WRITTEN. Choose with the end in view, because the end is not a mystery: "Declaring the end from the beginning, and from ancient times the things that are not yet done, saying, My counsel shall stand, and I will do all my pleasure" (Isaiah 46:10); "And, behold, I come quickly; and my reward is with me, to give every man according as his work shall be." (Revelation 22:12). THE WHOLE OF IT. His kings are bold, and they are HIS. There are two paths, and the tell is obedience rather than the word Lord. You cannot be His king unless you are born again, and you reign only after serving — because He is the King of kings, before whom crowned elders cast their crowns down. Guard the tongue that holds life and death. Create wealth His way, under covenant, never confusion. Win souls through excellence, because excellence is what earns the hearing. Draw the skill from His Word, studied comprehensively. And choose with the written destination in view. Kingship is received from Him and held in worship — never self-crowned.',
