      howToRun: 'Prayer + the anchor (5): read Revelation 1:6 and Matthew 7:13-14 aloud (KJV). | Recap (10): last week\'s boldness - where did we stand bold as a lion, and confess a fault to keep the account clear? | Teach the arc (20): His kings, received not self-made (Revelation 1:6) -> two paths, tested by obedience (Matthew 7:13-14; Luke 6:46) -> the \'unless\': born again and serve (John 3:3; Matthew 20:27) -> the King of kings we worship (Revelation 19:16; Revelation 4:10) -> life and death in the tongue (Proverbs 18:21) -> wealth Yahweh\'s Way, not confusion (Deuteronomy 8:18; 1 Corinthians 14:33) -> win souls by excellence (Proverbs 11:30; Colossians 3:23) -> skill from His Word (2 Timothy 2:15; Acts 17:11) -> destination already written (Isaiah 46:10; Revelation 22:12). | Do-it-now (20): each names ONE area they are still their own king (surrender it), ONE word to change from death/confusion to life/truth, ONE act of excellence that could win a soul, and ONE Scripture study they will take up comprehensively this week. | Discussion (15): the prompts below. | Send-off (5): bow to be crowned - worship the King, guard the tongue, work with excellence, and study His Word with the written destination in view.',
