    facilitator: {
      talkingPoints: [
        'WORD FIRST / Darrell brought this (2026-08-30): \'wise as serpents\' = know the enemy without becoming him; deny the flesh; why the Word divides soul from spirit; capable but only Yahweh\'s will; lean not on our understanding; acknowledge Him - one way. Adversary named low; Yahweh and the Lion of Judah high. Every verse verbatim KJV.',
        'Both halves: wise unto good, simple (harmless) concerning evil (Matthew 10:16; Romans 16:19). Know the enemy Yahweh exposed and defeated - he only bruised the heel (Genesis 3:15; 1 Peter 5:8; Ephesians 6:11-13; John 8:44).',
        'The roaring lion is a counterfeit - he comes AS a lion (1 Peter 5:8); never confuse him with the true Lion of Judah who prevailed (Revelation 5:5; Genesis 49:9). Keep the wisdom holy, not carnal (James 3:15,17; 4:7).',
        'Deny the flesh - his ground (Matthew 16:24; Galatians 5:16-17,24; Romans 8:13; 2 Corinthians 10:5; Matthew 15:19); and the Word divides soul from spirit so you discern flesh from Spirit and follow the Spirit (Hebrews 4:12; Romans 8:14).',
        'Capable but only Yahweh\'s will, holy and whole - Jesus could call legions but did the Father\'s will (Matthew 26:53; John 5:30; 1 Peter 1:16); lean not on your own understanding, acknowledge Him, and He directs the ONE way (Proverbs 3:5-6; John 14:6; Matthew 7:14). Companion to L102, L104, L105.',
      ],
      howToRun: 'Prayer + the anchor (5): read Matthew 10:16 and Romans 16:19 aloud (KJV). | Recap (10): L105 - reading is not doing; where did we DO the Word this week? | Teach the arc (20): wise AND harmless (Matthew 10:16; Romans 16:19) -> know the enemy Yahweh exposed (Genesis 3:15; 1 Peter 5:8; Ephesians 6:11-13) -> the roaring lion is not the Lion of Judah (1 Peter 5:8 vs Revelation 5:5) -> serpent-wisdom not serpent-nature (James 3:15-17; 4:7) -> deny the flesh, his ground (Matthew 16:24; 2 Corinthians 10:5) -> the Word divides soul from spirit so we discern (Hebrews 4:12; Romans 8:14) -> capable but only Yahweh\'s will (Matthew 26:53; John 5:30; 1 Peter 1:16) -> lean not on our understanding, acknowledge Him, one way (Proverbs 3:5-6; John 14:6). | Do-it-now (20): each names ONE place they have been naive (dove without serpent) or carnal (serpent without dove); ONE fleshly pull/thought to deny and take captive; and ONE step to acknowledge Him and let Him direct. | Discussion (15): the prompts below. | Send-off (5): resist the devil (James 4:7), acknowledge Him, and walk the one way.',
      discussionPrompts: [
        '\'Wise as serpents, harmless as doves\' (Matthew 10:16). Are you more tempted to be naive (dove without serpent - not discerning the enemy) or carnal (serpent without dove - shrewd but corrupt) - and what does \'wise unto good, simple concerning evil\' (Romans 16:19) change?',
        'Remember that the devil comes AS a roaring lion (1 Peter 5:8) - a counterfeit of the Lion of Judah (Revelation 5:5). Where has a roar (fear, threat, accusation) made you forget the real Lion already prevailed - and what does resisting him (James 4:7) look like there?',
        'Darrell asked why the Word divides soul from spirit (Hebrews 4:12). Name a recent pull you now see was FLESH, not the Spirit. How would denying that flesh (Matthew 16:24; 2 Corinthians 10:5) and acknowledging Him (Proverbs 3:6) put you back on the one way?',
      ],
    },
