      howToRun: 'Sixty to seventy-five minutes. OPEN (5) by reading the six claims of the clip aloud, flatly, without commentary, and asking only: which of these could be checked, and how? Do not answer yet. WORD FIRST (15): read Proverbs 31:30, 1 Samuel 16:7 and John 7:24 and establish the test Yahweh actually gives - then ask the room to find the credential in it, in either direction. There is none. THE MEASURE (10): read Exodus 20:16, Leviticus 19:16, Proverbs 11:1 and 20:10 and let the room sit with a statistic being weighed as testimony. THE CHECK (15): run the four questions on the ninety-seven percent together, then read movement 5 and movement 6 in one pass, tier 1 first and the true parts immediately after - never one without the other. THE OVER-REACH (15): movements 8 and 9, walking through Deborah, Huldah, Abigail, Priscilla, Lydia and Proverbs 31, then Hosea 4:6 and Luke 10:42 for the mirror-image filter. THE MIRROR (10): movement 10 applied to everyone present, then movement 11 for the men. CLOSE (5) with Matthew 7:16,20 and Proverbs 31:30, and send them out with the in-app action - the next number they are handed this week. For a mixed-age or family setting run the child level as the whole lesson: numbers you cannot check, hearts you cannot see from outside, fruit you can watch, and learning as a gift.',
