          answer: 2,
          explain: 'All three from the Word. The guarded heart of Proverbs 4:23 stands beside love that "Beareth all things, believeth all things, hopeth all things, endureth all things." (1 Corinthians 13:7). Vengeance is not ours: "avenge not yourselves, but rather give place unto wrath" (Romans 12:19). And "Cursed be the man that trusteth in man, and maketh flesh his arm" (Jeremiah 17:5) — asking a person to settle your worth seats a creature where only the Creator belongs. It will crush them and never satisfy you.',
