    title: 'The People of Judah and the People of the Way — Who They Are, Where They Are, and Whom to Listen To',
    bigIdea: 'THE QUESTION, ASKED 2026-09-09. Darrell asked: who and where are the people of Judah — Yehudah — and the people of the Way? They were, are and will be a tribe; the one tribe drawn from every nation, the humans who agree. And then the harder half: what about the historical events, the timelines, and accuracy about whom to listen to, from the Scriptures and the history we can process? THE WORD ANSWERS IN ORDER. Judah is a man named praise (Genesis 29:35), a tribe, the kingdom that kept David’s house, and the people the Word calls Jews — and the Word itself carries their timeline: split, Assyria, Babylon, return, the King, Rome. Where are the tribes? Scattered, never lost: "I will sift the house of Israel among all nations, like as corn is sifted in a sieve, yet shall not the least grain fall upon the earth." (Amos 9:9) James wrote "to the twelve tribes which are scattered abroad" (James 1:1) and the Lamb still seals them by name (Revelation 7:4). The Way is what the first believers were called (Acts 9:2; 24:14), and the name is His: "I am the way" (John 14:6). Darrell’s instinct has a precedent the Word wrote down: Caleb the Kenezite is counted "Of the tribe of Judah" (Numbers 13:6) "because that he wholly followed the LORD" (Joshua 14:14); Ruth and Rahab stand in the King’s own line (Matthew 1:5). The people of the Way from every nation are grafted INTO Israel’s tree (Romans 11:17), made "fellowcitizens with the saints" (Ephesians 2:19), "Abraham’s seed" (Galatians 3:29), "an holy nation" (1 Peter 2:9) — joined to the tribes, never replacing them: "Boast not against the branches." (Romans 11:18) And whom to listen to has one answer with a test attached: "This is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased; hear ye him" (Matthew 17:5) — "To the law and to the testimony: if they speak not according to this word, it is because there is no light in them." (Isaiah 8:20) AND IN THE PSYCHOLOGICAL WAR — psyops, liars, a world that "deceiveth" (Revelation 12:9) and even lies about who is a Jew (Revelation 3:9) — the tribe is still seen, by the marks He gave and no other: their Ways ("by their fruits ye shall know them", Matthew 7:20), their suffering for His name (Revelation 12:17), and above all, as Darrell put it in two words, known by love: "By this shall all men know that ye are my disciples, if ye have love one to another." (John 13:35) And the loving are still slaughtered by the warmongers — "we are accounted as sheep for the slaughter. Nay, in all these things we are more than conquerors" (Romans 8:36-37) — unless their Ways align ("When a man’s ways please the LORD, he maketh even his enemies to be at peace with him", Proverbs 16:7) and Yahweh raises them, over governments that frame "mischief by a law" (Psalms 94:20): "he putteth down one, and setteth up another." (Psalms 75:7)',
    inApp: 'This week, take one voice you are tempted to follow because of who they say they are — a lineage, a tribe, a nation, a title — and run the Word’s test on it instead: "To the law and to the testimony: if they speak not according to this word, it is because there is no light in them." (Isaiah 8:20) Then read Acts 24:14 and say what the Way actually is: "believing all things which are written in the law and in the prophets". Tap any reference in this lesson to read it in place. Genealogy is not the test; the Word is.',
    anchor: { ref: 'Amos 9:9; Romans 11:17-18; Matthew 17:5', theme: 'KJV: "I will sift the house of Israel among all nations, like as corn is sifted in a sieve, yet shall not the least grain fall upon the earth." (Amos 9:9) — scattered, never lost. "thou, being a wild olive tree, wert graffed in among them... Boast not against the branches." (Romans 11:17-18) — joined, never replacing. "This is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased; hear ye him." (Matthew 17:5) — the One to listen to.' },
