      'Gives Darrell’s instinct its precedent from the Word: Caleb the Kenezite counted "Of the tribe of Judah" (Numbers 13:6) "because that he wholly followed the LORD" (Joshua 14:14); Ruth the Moabitess ("thy people shall be my people, and thy God my God", Ruth 1:16) and Rahab in the King’s own line (Matthew 1:5); the stranger "as one that is born in the land" (Exodus 12:48); "this man was born there" (Psalms 87:6).',
      'Draws the Word’s own line between joined and replaced: grafted in "among them" (Romans 11:17), "Boast not against the branches" (Romans 11:18), the natural branches "beloved for the fathers’ sakes" (Romans 11:28) and to be grafted in again (Romans 11:23-24) — one fold, one Shepherd (John 10:16), never a second Israel.',
