      'Keeps Judah’s honour where the Word puts it: "unto them were committed the oracles of God" (Romans 3:2); "to the Jew first" (Romans 1:16); "salvation is of the Jews" (John 4:22); the nations take hold of a Jew "for we have heard that God is with you" (Zechariah 8:23) — the condition is stated in the verse.',
      'Reads the two untils on the same frame as Genesis 49:10: "until the times of the Gentiles be fulfilled" (Luke 21:24) and "until the fulness of the Gentiles be come in" (Romans 11:25) — and the gathering promised after: Deuteronomy 30:3-4; Isaiah 11:12; Ezekiel 37:21-22; Hosea 1:10-11; "And so all Israel shall be saved" (Romans 11:26).',
      'Names the psychological war from the Word — the lie has a father (John 8:44), disguises itself as light (2 Corinthians 11:14), deceives the whole world (Revelation 12:9), inverts good and evil (Isaiah 5:20), and even forges identity: "which say they are Jews, and are not, but do lie" (Revelation 3:9) — and shows the defence: "the love of the truth" (2 Thessalonians 2:10), "neither fear ye their fear" (Isaiah 8:12), every thought captive (2 Corinthians 10:5).',
      'Gives Darrell’s marks for seeing the tribe in the Word’s words: their Ways — "by their fruits ye shall know them" (Matthew 7:20; 1 John 3:10); their suffering — for Israel His correction in measure (Amos 3:2; Jeremiah 30:11), for the Way hatred for His name (Matthew 10:22; Revelation 12:17); and above all known by love — "By this shall all men know that ye are my disciples, if ye have love one to another." (John 13:35)',
      'Meets the hardest edge Darrell named — warmongering versus loving, the loving still slaughtered — with the Word’s own order: "we are accounted as sheep for the slaughter. Nay, in all these things we are more than conquerors" (Romans 8:36-37); the condition, "When a man’s ways please the LORD, he maketh even his enemies to be at peace with him" (Proverbs 16:7); the raising His, not the state’s — "he putteth down one, and setteth up another" (Psalms 75:7), "though he were dead, yet shall he live" (John 11:25); and the undermining named, a throne "which frameth mischief by a law" (Psalms 94:20).',
      'Answers keep the Way to live good and longsuffering under stolen wages from the Word: "What man is he that desireth life, and loveth many days, that he may see good?" (Psalms 34:12); "the cries of them which have reaped are entered into the ears of the Lord of sabaoth" (James 5:4); Jacob under Laban, "changed my wages ten times; but God suffered him not to hurt me" (Genesis 31:7); "for ye serve the Lord Christ" (Colossians 3:24).',
      'Answers which country stands against Yahweh’s Ways with the measure, not a flag — "Righteousness exalteth a nation: but sin is a reproach to any people" (Proverbs 14:34); Jeremiah 18:7-10 applied live — and names the laws the Word judges (Exodus 21:16; Deuteronomy 23:15). Then Harriet Tubman as established history: hunted by her own country’s law, she kept the Way, delivered the captives, and died still believing — Hebrews 11:13; Revelation 2:10; Revelation 14:13.',
      'Names the motive Darrell named from the Word’s own inventory: Babylon’s merchandise ends "and slaves, and souls of men" (Revelation 18:13); "the love of money is the root of all evil" (1 Timothy 6:10); "Ye have condemned and killed the just" (James 5:6) — and sets beside it those who kept Jesus as Lord under duress: "But if not... we will not serve thy gods" (Daniel 3:18); "Esteeming the reproach of Christ greater riches than the treasures in Egypt" (Hebrews 11:26).',
      'Answers because we aren’t loved with the verse where Israel asked it and He answered by name: "I have loved you, saith the LORD. Yet ye say, Wherein hast thou loved us?" (Malachi 1:2) — chosen "because the LORD loved you" (Deuteronomy 7:8), "with an everlasting love" (Jeremiah 31:3), "graven thee upon the palms of my hands" (Isaiah 49:16), "We love him, because he first loved us" (1 John 4:19); and names the selling (Deuteronomy 28:68; Joel 3:6) and the respect of persons (James 2:9) the Word judges.',
