      howToRun: 'Sixty minutes. Ten on the parable of the two weights, read aloud, with the question left open of who in the story actually lost — press until somebody says the merchant’s own sons. Fifteen on the Scripture cluster, reading Deuteronomy 25:13-15, Proverbs 11:1 and Proverbs 13:23 together so the room sees the command, the classification and the economic consequence side by side. Fifteen on the evidence, stated plainly, with matched-pair testing explained carefully because it is the piece that removes the usual counter-argument. Ten on the correction, delivered as a worked example of checking a claim you already believe, ending on esusu and the inheritance. Ten on Nehemiah and the close. If the room is older, make space for the testimony — several will have their own version of the hand that went in, and those accounts are evidence, not anecdote. Do not let the hour end on the grievance; the last ten minutes belong to the instrument AND to the two ways. Finish with Joshua putting the choice to the people and naming what his own house would do — a room that leaves accused will not act, and a room that leaves chosen will.',
