      howToRun: 'Sixty minutes. Ten on the parable of the seventh year, read aloud, ending on the sentence about the open doorway; leave a pause there rather than explaining it. Twenty on the passage itself — Exodus 21:2-6 and Deuteronomy 15:12-17 read consecutively by three different voices, then the three provisions named on a board. Ten on the price, using the two-ledgers story, with silver and gold named and refused. Ten on the upgrade: servant, friend, son, heir, in His own words. Five on Romans 6:16 to close the autonomy exit. Five on Psalm 40 and Hebrews, unhurried, as the close. If somebody in the room has been mocked with this objection, they will likely say so during the passage reading; let that happen and do not rescue it too quickly. Send everyone out with the one question rather than with a summary.',
