        body: 'A prophet who had just called down fire sits under a juniper tree and asks to die. "It is enough; now, O LORD, take away my life; for I am not better than my fathers." Read what Heaven does next, because it is not what a religious house would do. No rebuke. No reminder of yesterday’s victory. No question about his faith. An angel touches him and says "Arise and eat." He eats, and lies back down. And the angel comes A SECOND TIME and says it again, and this time names the cause out loud: "Arise and eat; because the journey is too great for thee." The journey is too great for thee. Not your heart is wrong. Not you have lost your nerve. The load is bigger than the body carrying it. Then he walks forty days on the strength of that meal, and only after all of it does the voice come, and it is not in the wind or the earthquake or the fire: "a still small voice." The order is Yahweh’s own. Food, sleep, food again, then the word. A family that hands out correction to someone who has not slept or eaten is stricter than Yahweh, and less effective, because it is answering a body problem with a character speech. He knows what we are made of: "For he knoweth our frame; he remembereth that we are dust."',
