      'Where are you certain you understand something that the people around you can see you do not? Who would tell you, and have you ever actually asked them?',
      'Every way of a man is right in his own eyes. Ask your wife or husband what you say that hurts them and that you do not seem to notice — then say nothing until they finish. What did you hear?',
      'Husbands: dwell with them according to knowledge. What is one thing about your wife you do not know and should, and what will you do this week to learn it?',
      'Every idle word is accounted for, not only every cruel one. Which throwaway habit does that reach?',
      'Who within your reach is weary right now, and what would a word in season to them sound like this week?',
      'One sentence needs repairing, with no BUT in the repair. Who, and what will you say?',
      'Your mind predicts before people finish. Name one person you have a standing forecast of. When did you last let them contradict it?',
      'Secret faults are faults secret from YOU. Pray Psalm 139:23-24 and write what comes back. What did you not want on the page?',
      'The meek will he teach his way. Where is pride currently costing you sight — not reputation, SIGHT?',
      'Proverbs 2 sets four conditions: receive, incline, cry out, search as for silver. Which of the four are you actually doing, and which have you never done?',
      'Pick your cadence and put it somewhere you will see it: one Proverbs chapter a day for 31 days, or five Psalms a day. Which, starting when?',
      'If your spouse will not read the Word, the instrument is conduct BEHELD, not a case argued. What have you been trying to win by argument, and what would the demonstration version look like?',
      'Where are you carrying a verdict you believe is wrong? Commit it in prayer this week rather than answering it — and search it once for the one true detail before you set it down.',
      'Honest and hard: are you the mocked one, or the mocking one? Yahweh names both duties in one verse — love and reverence. Which is yours, and are you keeping it?',
      'If derision is aimed at the Word rather than at you, God is not mocked and the sowing returns to the sower. Does that change what you feel obliged to defend?',
      'Nehemiah answered once and went back to building. What is your one answer, and what is the building you should return to?',
      'Is the person you are frustrated with unwilling, or unable yet? Strong meat belongs to the full age, BY REASON OF USE. Which are you actually dealing with, and how would your approach differ if you were honest about it?',
      'The wrath of man worketh not the righteousness of God — it does not produce the result. Where have you been using frustration as a tool, and what has it actually produced?',
      'A man with no rule over his own spirit is a city without walls. Which provocation walks straight in every time?',
      'A wise man keeps it in TILL AFTERWARDS — he still says it, just later. What needs saying later rather than now?',
      'A just man falls seven times and is still called just. What recent failure have you been treating as a verdict?',
      'In due season we shall reap, IF WE FAINT NOT. Fainting is the only variable left to you. Where are you closest to fainting, and what would not-fainting look like this week?',
      'Yahweh fed Elijah and let him sleep BEFORE He corrected him, and named the cause as the journey being too great. Who in your house needs food and rest before they need a conversation — and have you been skipping straight to the conversation?',
      'Honest audit: how much of last week’s friction in your home followed a short night? Sleep loss raises reactivity and weakens the brake. What would protecting sleep cost you, and what is it already costing you?',
