        'Isaiah 28:13 says the same lines, refused, become the fall. Is there a precept you have been reading and not running, and what has it cost so far?',
        'The chapter and verse numbers were added by men — Langton, Estienne. Does that change how you read? What do you now understand the Word to be, apart from its numbers?',
        'James 1:22 — doers, not hearers only. Name one line you have heard a hundred times and never executed. What would running it once, today, actually look like?',
        '2 Timothy 3:16 as a panel: doctrine the setpoint, reproof the alarm, correction the actuator, instruction the schedule. Which of the four is your weakest, and who in this group could help you tune it?',
        'Jesus taught with seeds, sheep and bread because the hearers already owned them (Matthew 13:34). What known thing from your own trade or home could carry the Word to someone who does not know Him yet?',
        'Genesis 2:15 — dress it and keep it. What corner of His program has He put you at the panel of, and are you operating it or letting it drift?',
        'The lesson says a controller cannot love the building, but He loves the world He wrote. Where has your picture of Him gone cold and mechanical, and which verse in this lesson warms it back up?',
