    bigIdea: 'FOLLOW THE LEADER. You are following something already — a feed, a camp, a voice you did not choose — so the only live question is who. The Leader came up in neither of the religious camps of His day and they could not place His training: "How knoweth this man letters, having never learned?" (John 7:15). His own town would not have Him and tried to throw Him off a hill the same afternoon (Luke 4:28-29). He is a Shepherd with a death clause in the job description — "the good shepherd giveth his life for the sheep" (John 10:11) — and Peter names the jurisdiction: "the Shepherd and Bishop of your souls" (1 Peter 2:25). He had never known pain and took a body that could feel it, "a man of sorrows, and acquainted with grief" (Isaiah 53:3). Nobody took His life: "I lay it down of myself" (John 10:18), on a piece of wood, "while we were yet sinners" (Romans 5:8). He had twelve legions on call and opened not His mouth (Matthew 26:53; Isaiah 53:7), because meek is power under command and it inherits the earth (Matthew 5:5). He grieves, He weeps, He sings over you (Genesis 6:6; John 11:35; Zephaniah 3:17), and He is jealous FOR you (Zechariah 1:14). The men with the money killed Him the week He turned their tables — read Mark 11:15, 11:17 and then 11:18 in order. The government is on HIS shoulder (Isaiah 9:6), so cast the burden and take His yoke. And here is the deepest thing: Yahweh never lacked power or instant obedience — "he spake, and it was done" (Psalm 33:9). What nothing that merely executes can give Him is a being who suffered first and still said Thy will be done, and that being is offered His throne (Revelation 3:21; 2 Timothy 2:12). Why any of it works: "We love him, because he first loved us" (1 John 4:19).',
